; Exhaustiveness one constructor down, with the column's own type.
;
; The matrix spliced a constructor's declared field types into the
; inner column as written, so over `(Option (Option Int))` the inner
; column was the declaration's `a` - a type no constructor set
; enumerates - and only a binder could cover it. A complete nested
; match was therefore AX3005 "some values are not covered" (the QA
; sweep's lead, confirmed 2026-08-21), and an incomplete one could
; not name what it lacked. `matCtorsExh` substitutes the column's
; arguments now (`tyEnvSubst`, which mints nothing).
;
;   line 20: `(Some (Some x))` and `(None)` - the inner `None` is
;            what is missing, and is what is named            AX3005
;   line 26: the same over a user type, `MNil` inside `MCons`  AX3005
;
; `deep` and `both` emit nothing: every value is covered.
(data MyList a
  (MNil)
  (MCons a (MyList a)))

(:: partial (-> (Option (Option Int)) Int))

(fn (partial o)
  (match o
    ((Some (Some x)) 1)
    ((None) 0)
  )
)

(:: deep (-> (Option (Option Int)) Int))

(fn (deep o)
  (match o
    ((Some (Some x)) (+ x 1))
    ((Some (None)) 1)
    ((None) 0)
  )
)

(:: two (-> (MyList Int) Int))

(fn (two l)
  (match l
    ((MCons h (MCons h2 t)) 2)
    ((MNil) 0)
  )
)

(:: both (-> (MyList Int) Int))

(fn (both l)
  (match l
    ((MCons h (MCons h2 t)) 2)
    ((MCons h (MNil)) 1)
    ((MNil) 0)
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
